  "title": "Women's March on Versailles",
  "summary": "On 5 October 1789 crowds of Parisian market women marched to Versailles over bread prices and anger at a royal bodyguards' banquet. They besieged the palace, received promises from Louis XVI through a delegation, and the royal family left Versailles for Paris on 6 October. World History Encyclopedia calls it a blow to absolute monarchy.",
